```
By using the `as` keyword, you're telling the type system that you're certain that `value` is a string, even though the type system can't guarantee it. This is called a "type assertion".

Note that this is different from a type cast, which would change the type of the value at runtime. A type assertion is just a hint to the type system, and it doesn't change the actual type of the value.

